.TH USBRADIOPLUS.CONF 5 "August 2026" "USBRadioPlus alpha" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
usbradioplus.conf \- USBRadioPlus radio-interface configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/asterisk/usbradioplus.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file contains one
.B [general]
section followed by one named section for each USB radio interface.  Values in
.B [general]
become defaults for each interface.  A device section overrides those values.
The section name forms the Asterisk channel name; section
.B [usb]
is addressed as
.BR RadioPlus/usb .
.PP
Option names are not case sensitive.  Boolean values are
.B yes
or
.BR no .
Unless stated otherwise, times are milliseconds and frequencies are hertz.
.SH JITTER BUFFER
The standard Asterisk channel jitter-buffer options may be placed in
.BR [general] .
.TP
.B jbenable = yes|no
Enable a receive-side jitter buffer.  Default is
.BR no .
.TP
.B jbmaxsize = milliseconds
Maximum jitter-buffer length.  Default is 200.
.TP
.B jbresyncthreshold = milliseconds
Timestamp discontinuity that causes resynchronization.  Default is 1000.
.TP
.B jbimpl = fixed|adaptive
Select the fixed-size or adaptive implementation.  Default is
.BR fixed .
.TP
.B jblog = yes|no
Write jitter-buffer frame diagnostics.  Default is
.BR no .
.SH DEVICE SELECTION AND USB AUDIO
.TP
.B devstr = string
Select a USB audio device by its ALSA device string.  Normally set by the tuning
utility.
.TP
.B serial = string
Bind the section to a USB interface serial number.  Use this on systems with
more than one interface.
.TP
.B hdwtype = 0|1
Select the interface wiring.  Use 0 for the usual modified USB sound fob and 1
for a Dingotel/Sph interface.  Default is 0.
.PP
When the selected interface provides a CM1xx input attenuator, the driver
always bypasses it.
.TP
.B eeprom = 0|1
Read and write tuning values in a supported interface EEPROM.  Default is 1.
.TP
.B frags = integer
Requested USB audio fragment count.  Change only when diagnosing a driver or
latency problem.  Default is the driver build value.
.TP
.B queuesize = integer
Maximum queued output fragments.  Default is 20.
.TP
.B rxcpusaver = yes|no
Reduce receive processing while the receiver is closed.
.TP
.B txcpusaver = yes|no
Reduce transmit processing while the transmitter is idle.
.SH RECEIVER AND SQUELCH
.TP
.B rxdemod = no|speaker|flat
Describe the receiver audio connection.  Use
.B flat
for discriminator audio requiring de-emphasis,
.B speaker
for audio already de-emphasized by the receiver, or
.B no
when receive audio is unused.
.TP
.B carrierfrom = no|usb|usbinvert|dsp|vox|pp|ppinvert
Choose the carrier-operated-squelch source:
.B usb
and
.B usbinvert
use the interface input;
.B dsp
uses the noise detector;
.B vox
uses received voice energy; and
.B pp
or
.B ppinvert
uses the parallel port.
This setting is used when
.B hardware_cos_assignment
is absent from usbradioplus-processing.conf.
.TP
.B voxhangtime = integer
Hold carrier detection after VOX energy ends.  Default is 2000.
.TP
.B rxsqvox = integer
VOX detector threshold adjustment.
.TP
.B rxsqhyst = integer
Hysteresis for DSP carrier detection.  Default is 3000.
.TP
.B rxnoisefiltype = integer
Select the DSP noise-detector filter.  This is an advanced calibration setting.
.TP
.B rxsquelchdelay = integer
Delay receive program audio so the driver can remove a carrier-squelch tail.
.TP
.B rxondelay = integer
After PTT releases, ignore carrier for this many 20 ms intervals.  Use on a
simplex station to prevent relay racing.  Default is 0.
.TP
.B txoffdelay = integer
After PTT releases, ignore the receiver for this many 20 ms intervals.  This can
exclude a linked repeater's transmitter hang time.  Default is 0.
.TP
.B rxpolarity = yes|no
Invert the received radio-signaling bit polarity.
.SH CTCSS AND OTHER LOW-SPEED SIGNALING
.TP
.B ctcssfrom = no|usb|usbinvert|dsp|pp|ppinvert
Choose the receive CTCSS indication source.  The
.B dsp
setting decodes tones from flat receiver audio;
.B usb
and
.B usbinvert
use the interface input; parallel-port forms use the configured input pin.
.TP
.B rxctcssfreqs = list
Comma-separated receive CTCSS tones.  Frequencies must be supported by the
decoder. This setting is used when
.B hardware_rx_ctcss_frequencies
is absent from usbradioplus-processing.conf.
.TP
.B txctcssfreqs = list
Comma-separated transmit CTCSS tones corresponding to the receive list. This
setting is used when
.B hardware_tx_ctcss_frequencies
is absent from usbradioplus-processing.conf.
.TP
.B txctcssdefault = frequency
Tone transmitted when no received tone selects another entry.
.TP
.B rxctcssoverride = yes|no
Begin in carrier-squelch operation without requiring a decoded CTCSS tone.
.TP
.B rxctcssrelax = integer
Select CTCSS decoder tolerance.  The normal setting is 1.
.TP
.B txtoctype = no|phase|notone
Choose CTCSS turn-off signaling:
.B no
drops PTT with the tone,
.B phase
sends a reverse burst, and
.B notone
removes tone before PTT.
.TP
.B dcsrxpolarity, dcstxpolarity = yes|no
Invert receive or transmit DCS polarity.
.TP
.B lsdrxpolarity, lsdtxpolarity = yes|no
Invert receive or transmit low-speed-data polarity.
.SH TRANSMIT ROUTING AND CONTROL
.TP
.B txprelim = yes|no
Apply transmit pre-emphasis and limiting for a direct modulator connection.
.TP
.B txlimonly = yes|no
Apply limiting without pre-emphasis, typically for a microphone input whose
radio supplies pre-emphasis.
.TP
.B txmixa, txmixb = no|voice|tone|composite|auxvoice
Select the signal on the left or right USB playback channel:
.B voice
is program audio,
.B tone
is CTCSS,
.B composite
combines both, and
.B auxvoice
is an unkeyed monitor feed.
These settings are used when the corresponding hardware output assignment is
absent from usbradioplus-processing.conf.
.TP
.B invertptt = yes|no
Invert the USB PTT output.  Default operation grounds the output to transmit.
.TP
.B duplex = 0|1
Select half-duplex or full-duplex radio-interface operation.
.TP
.B duplex3 = 0..999
Set local receiver-to-transmitter audio.  Zero disables the route and 999 is
full level.
.TP
.B duplex3mode = hardware|software
Use the CM119 hardware mixer or the 48 kHz software receiver path for the
.B duplex3
route.  Default is
.BR hardware .
.TP
.B txsettletime = integer
Delay transmit audio after asserting PTT so the transmitter can reach steady
operation.
.TP
.B txrxblankingtime = integer
Blank receive signaling around transmitter switching.
.TP
.B txpolarity = yes|no
Invert the transmitted radio-signaling bit polarity.
.SH AUDIO FILTERS
.TP
.B rxlpf, txlpf = no|yes|selector|frequency
Set the receive or transmit low-pass cutoff.
.TP
.B rxhpf, txhpf = no|yes|selector|frequency
Set the receive or transmit high-pass cutoff.
.PP
On transmit,
.B txhpf
sets the low-frequency edge and
.B txlpf
sets the high-frequency edge of one final brick-wall band-pass. They do not
create additional filter stages.
.PP
.B no
disables a filter and
.B yes
selects its 300 Hz high-pass or 3000 Hz low-pass default.  An integer selects
the standard radio filter: low-pass selectors 0, 1, and 2 are 3000, 3300, and
3500 Hz; high-pass selectors 0, 1, and 2 are 300, 250, and 120 Hz.  A decimal
number specifies the exact cutoff in hertz.  A high-pass cutoff must be lower
than its paired low-pass cutoff.
.PP
Useful initial passbands are 300--3000 Hz for 12.5 kHz narrowband and 15 kHz FM,
250--4000 Hz for 20 kHz FM, and 250--5000 Hz for 25 kHz FM.  Final settings must
be verified for intelligibility, CTCSS margin, peak deviation, and occupied
bandwidth with a service monitor.
.SH AUDIO-PATH CONTROLS
.TP
.B emphasis_corner_hz = frequency
Set the pre-emphasis and de-emphasis corner.  Default is 212.206590789 Hz,
corresponding to a 750 microsecond time constant.
.SH GPIO AND PARALLEL PORT
.TP
.B clipledgpio = 0..8
Pulse the selected GPIO for 500 ms when the receive ADC clips.  Zero disables
the indication.
.TP
.B gpio1 ... gpio8 = in|out0|out1
Configure a CM1xx GPIO as an input or as an output with its initial state.
.TP
.B pport = path
Set the parallel-port device.  Default is
.BR /dev/parport0 .
Legacy binary channel selection uses data pins 6 through 9.  RTX synthesizer
programming uses data pins 2 through 6.  Pins used for either purpose must not
also be assigned as general-purpose outputs.
.TP
.B pbase = address
Set a parallel-port I/O base address when no device driver is used.
.TP
.B pp2 ... pp9 = out0|out1|ptt
Configure a parallel-port output pin and its initial state or assign it to PTT.
.TP
.B pp10, pp12, pp13, pp15 = in|cor|ctcss
Configure a parallel-port input and optionally assign it to carrier or CTCSS.
.SH REMOTE AND DIAGNOSTIC OPTIONS
.TP
.B rxfreq, txfreq = integer
Set receive and transmit frequency in Hz for a legacy parallel-programmed RTX
radio.  A value of zero disables synthesizer programming.  USBRadioPlus writes
the synthesizer before changing the physical PTT output.  A remote
.B SETFREQ
command supplies temporary frequencies while remote-base operation is active.
.TP
.B radioactive = yes|no
Enable remote radio control for this channel.
.TP
.B rptnum = integer
Associate the radio with an app_rpt node number for remote operation.
.TP
.B area = integer
Set the remote-control area identifier.
.TP
.B ukey = string
Set the remote-control authentication key.
.TP
.B idleinterval = integer
Set the remote-radio idle polling interval.
.TP
.B turnoffs = integer
Set the remote-radio turn-off behavior mask.
.TP
.B sendvoter = integer
Send receiver information to the configured voter path.
.TP
.B tracetype = integer
Select DSP trace output.
.TP
.B tracelevel = integer
Set DSP diagnostic verbosity.
.TP
.B fever = integer
Enable low-level diagnostic behavior used by the tuning interface.
.SH TUNING VALUES
These values are normally written by
.BR usbradioplus-tune (8).
.TP
.B rxmixerset = 0..999
Set the USB capture mixer level when
.B hardware_input_gain_db
is absent.
.TP
.B rxvoiceadj = number
Set recovered voice level when the local-chain
.B input_gain_db
option is absent from
.BR usbradioplus-processing.conf (5).
The value is converted to decibels; 0.5 is unity.
.TP
.B rxsquelchadj = 0..999
Set the DSP carrier-squelch threshold.
.TP
.B txmixaset, txmixbset = 0..999
Set left- and right-channel USB playback levels when the corresponding hardware
output gain is absent from usbradioplus-processing.conf.
.TP
.B txctcssadj = 0..999
Set transmitted CTCSS deviation.
.TP
.B txslimsp = 5000..13000
Set the transmitter soft-limiter onset used when transmit limiting is selected.
.SH FILES
.B /etc/asterisk/usbradioplus.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR usbradioplus (7),
.BR usbradioplus-processing.conf (5),
.BR usbradioplus-tune (8),
.BR rpt.conf (5)
